cards.notes:
POST-LAUNCH. Carded by WF-07 (R4), which requires it explicitly: 'Card the staff-assisted activation path as post-launch.'

WHY IT IS NEEDED. WF-07 links a patient only when EXACTLY ONE live row (deleted_at null, merged_into_id null, auth_user_id null) carries the proven phone. Every other case refuses with a generic pt-PT message directing the patient to the clinic. Those refusals are correct and they are also real people who cannot log in:
- a shared household number on two patient rows (multi-match);
- a patient whose clinic row holds an old or wrong phone (zero-match);
- a patient with a duplicate row already claimed (already-linked);
- a patient with no phone on file at all.

The refusal path is the SAFE half and it ships with LOOP 3. This card is the other half: a staff-side way for reception to resolve the identity in person and link the row deliberately. Until it exists, the answer to a refused patient is a phone call to the clinic, which is what the copy already says.

DO NOT BUILD IT AS AN OTP BYPASS. Whatever this becomes, it may not mint a session from anything but a proven phone (Decision D), and it must leave an audit row naming the staff member who performed the link - the same reasoning that makes the patient audit log append-only. A staff-assisted link is exactly the operation an attacker would target.

SCHEDULING: post-launch, excluded from the Wave 13 loop order. It does not gate PG1.
